THE THREE-DAY SEALING PROCESS
Timing and conduct reference for a full extraction.

An extraction is not swift. Drawing a tailed beast whole from its host and binding it
into the Gedo Statue takes three days and three nights of continuous sealing. Plan
accordingly.

Day 1: The Statue is summoned and all ten rings take station. The Illusionary Dragon
seizes the beast's chakra. The host begins to weaken as extraction takes hold.
Day 2: The beast is drawn out steadily. Bearers must maintain the technique without
break; projected members hold their locations. The host nears death.
Day 3: The final measure of the beast is pulled into the Statue. A new eye opens. The
host expires as the last of the beast leaves the body.

Requirements throughout:
- Uninterrupted attendance of all ten rings. A dropped position endangers the seal.
- A secured, hidden chamber. Barriers up, Zetsu on watch.
- No engagement with intruders inside the chamber during the process if avoidable.

Three days is the cost of every beast. There is no faster path. Guard the time.
